```csharp
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Create a new HttpWebRequest object for the target URL.
        HttpWebRequest request = (HttpWebRequest)WebRequest.Create("https://example.com/api/resource");

        // Set the method to POST.
        request.Method = "POST";

        // Set the content type to JSON.
        request.ContentType = "application/json";

        // Load the client certificate from a file.
        X509Certificate2 cert = new X509Certificate2("path/to/client/certificate.pfx", "password");

        // Add the client certificate to the request.
        request.ClientCertificates.Add(cert);

        // Write the request body as JSON.
        string requestBody = "{\"key\":\"value\"}";
        byte[] requestBodyBytes = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(requestBody);
        request.ContentLength = requestBodyBytes.Length;

        using (Stream requestStream = request.GetRequestStream())
        {
            requestStream.Write(requestBodyBytes, 0, requestBodyBytes.Length);
        }

        // Send the request and get the response.
        using (HttpWebResponse response = (HttpWebResponse)request.GetResponse())
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Response status code: {0}", response.StatusCode);
        }
    }
}
```
In this example, we create a new `HttpWebRequest` object for the target URL and set the method to POST. We then load the client certificate from a file using the `X509Certificate2` class and add it to the request using the `ClientCertificates` property.

We write the request body as JSON and send the request using the `GetRequestStream` and `Write` methods. Finally, we send the request and get the response using the `GetResponse` method.

Note that you will need to replace `"https://example.com/api/resource"` with the actual URL of the API endpoint you want to call, and `"path/to/client/certificate.pfx"` and `"password"` with the path to your client certificate file and its password, respectively. You may also need to adjust the request body and other settings depending on the specific requirements of the API you are calling.

To extract hashtags from a given text in C#, you can use regular expressions (regex). Here's an example of how to do it:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string inputText = "This is a sample text with #hashtags and #moreHashtags.";

        // Define the regex pattern for matching hashtags
        string hashtagPattern = @"#\w+";

        // Use Regex.Matches to find all matches in the input text
        MatchCollection matches = Regex.Matches(inputText, hashtagPattern);

        Console.WriteLine("Extracted Hashtags:");
        foreach (Match match in matches)
        {
            Console.WriteLine(match.Value);
        }
    }
}
```

In this code:
- We define a `hashtagPattern` that matches any word starting with a hash symbol (`#`) followed by one or more word characters (`\w+`).
- The `Regex.Matches` method finds all occurrences of the pattern in the input text.
- Finally, we iterate through the matched results and print each hashtag.

When you run this program with the provided input text, it will output:
```
Extracted Hashtags:
#hashtags
#moreHashtags
```

This approach ensures that only valid hashtags are extracted from the text.

